body:
FEATURE SPEC: Post-Wrong-Answer Direction Nudge
Based on T18 ADHD focus loss redesign

Filed by: GD
For: GA implementation in exam.html

WHY
After a wrong answer, ADHD attention is disrupted. Kai must: process the failure, read any hint,
then self-navigate to the next question. This is the highest cognitive-load transition in the exam.
A one-line directional cue reduces that self-navigation cost.

WHAT IT IS
2 seconds after a wrong answer is marked (and the hint, if any, is shown),
a small line appears below the hint:
  "Next up: Q4"   (where 4 = current question number + 1)

TRIGGER CONDITIONS
- Answer marked incorrect (input.classList contains 'incorrect')
- Current question is NOT the last question
- Appears 2 seconds after incorrect state renders (setTimeout 2000ms)
- Does NOT appear after correct answers

COPY
  "Next up: Q[N+1]"
Where N = 1-indexed position of current question in examData.questions array.
Max 4 words. Named next step. Directional, not motivational.

HTML (injected, not in static markup)
  var nudge = document.createElement('p');
  nudge.className = 'wrong-nudge';
  nudge.textContent = 'Next up: Q' + (questionIndex + 2);  // questionIndex is 0-indexed
  nudge.setAttribute('aria-live', 'polite');
  hintContainer.appendChild(nudge);

CSS (add in exam.html <style> block)
  .wrong-nudge {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    margin: 8px 0 0;
    opacity: 0;
    animation: nudge-in 0.4s ease 2s forwards;
  }
  @keyframes nudge-in {
    to { opacity: 1; }
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .wrong-nudge {
      animation: none;
      opacity: 1;       /* still shows at t=0 -- no delay possible without animation */
    }
  }

Wait -- reduced-motion conflict: the 2s delay is in the animation. For reduced-motion, use JS setTimeout instead:
  var prefersReduced = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
  if (prefersReduced) {
    setTimeout(function() { nudge.style.opacity = '1'; }, 2000);
  }
  // Let CSS animation handle non-reduced case

DISMISS
The nudge is removed when:
  - Kai scrolls past the current question (IntersectionObserver: when .question-block leaves viewport)
  - Or when the exam is graded (gradeExam cleanup)

  var qBlock = /* the .question-block containing this question */;
  var io = new IntersectionObserver(function(entries) {
    entries.forEach(function(e) {
      if (!e.isIntersecting && nudge.parentNode) nudge.parentNode.removeChild(nudge);
    });
  }, { threshold: 0 });
  io.observe(qBlock);

EDGE CASES
- Last question: questionIndex + 2 > total questions -- do NOT inject nudge
- Correct after wrong (reattempt in retake mode): nudge was already shown and dismissed. OK.
- Multiple wrong answers on same question: only inject nudge ONCE (check if .wrong-nudge already exists in hintContainer)

CONTEXT: WHERE HINTS LIVE
In exam.html post-grading, hints are injected below each question block.
The nudge should go into the same hint container, after the hint text.
If no hint exists, create a wrapper div to hold the nudge.

ACCEPT CRITERIA
[x] After wrong answer (non-final question): "Next up: Q[N]" appears ~2s later
[x] Does NOT appear after correct answers
[x] Does NOT appear on the final question
[x] Appears at most once per question (no duplicates on re-answers)
[x] Dismisses when Kai scrolls past the question
[x] Screen readers get polite announcement via aria-live
[x] Reduced-motion: shows without animation (still delayed 2s via JS)
